# Runtime Dev Branch Notes — Backend Adapter Contract v1

**Date:** 2026-06-15  
**Branch:** `backend-adapter-contract-v1`  
**Status:** Staged locally from the main mirror; syntax-checked, contract-smoke-tested, helper-checked, and artifact-guarded in sandbox. Not repo-verified on GitHub yet. No real-runtime test required if the branch remains contract-only and does not touch runtime/worker/lifecycle/native execution surfaces.

---

## Purpose

This branch adds a contract-only Backend Adapter layer under `runtime/backends/`.

The branch answers, in code and tests:

```text
how a backend adapter descriptor declares a stable adapterId and backendKind;
how adapter descriptors define capability/service/result/cancellation/stream expectations without executing anything;
how an adapter registry validates and exposes adapter descriptors;
how a backend adapter plan checks a capability service plan against matching adapter metadata;
how backend adapter contracts remain metadata-only and non-executing.
```

This is the next substrate step after the action envelope, capability registry, bus skeleton, capability router contract, and capability service contract branches:

```text
action envelope -> bus intake -> router plan -> service contract -> backend adapter contract -> executor
```

---

## Namespace decision

Backend adapter contracts live under:

```text
runtime/backends/
```

They were intentionally not added under `runtime/bus/`.

Reason:

```text
runtime/bus/ is the controlled action boundary and remains bus-related.
Backend adapters are downstream replaceable execution mechanisms selected after bus/router/service approval.
runtime/backends/ keeps the modular substrate layers readable before future executor work exists.
```

