## Modular design shape

The branch follows the split service-contract pattern:

```text
backendAdapterCommon.mjs          shared constants/copy/prefix/guard helpers
backendAdapterDefinition.mjs      adapter metadata definition validation
backendAdapterRegistry.mjs        adapter registry validation and lookup helpers
backendAdapterPlan.mjs            service-plan-to-adapter-plan validation
backendAdapterContract.mjs        small public barrel/export surface
```

The public import surface is the barrel:

```js
import {
    assertBackendAdapterDefinition,
    assertBackendAdapterRegistry,
    assertBackendAdapterPlan
} from "./runtime/backends/backendAdapterContract.mjs";
```

---

## Contract-only guardrails

Backend adapter descriptors are metadata-only. They reject:

```text
modelPath/baseModel/mmprojPath/projectorPath fields
backendOptions/adapterArgs/rawBackendPayload fields
toolProcess/command/shell/exec/spawn/cwd/env/stdio fields
function/handler/execute/executeAction/invoke fields
path-like metadata values
unknown top-level and nested fields
prototype-pollution keys
```

The plan helper returns a descriptor:

```js
const backendAdapterPlan = {
    contractVersion: "backend-adapter.v1",
    servicePlan,
    adapter
};
```

It does not call a service, call a backend, enqueue a request, emit runtime events, stream tokens, or touch native/model execution.

---

## Validation coverage

New smoke test:

```bash
node ./tests/smokeTestBackendAdapterContract.mjs
```

Coverage includes:

```text
valid adapter descriptor normalization/copying;
unknown top-level and nested field rejection;
prototype-pollution and execution/process/payload key rejection;
model/projector/path-like key and value rejection;
invalid/unselectable status rejection;
registry duplicate adapterId rejection;
multiple adapters for the same backendKind with different adapterId values;
copy-on-read list/get behavior;
valid service plan + matching adapter plan;
missing backend adapter rejection;
backendKind/capability/service compatibility rejection;
modelBundleId/hardwareProfileId adapter requirement rejection;
streaming/cancellation/timeout compatibility rejection;
error-normalization compatibility rejection;
descriptor-only plan output checks.
```

